WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.063
Meet BulkAuto:

00:00:03.063 --> 00:00:05.470
bulk cleanup for QuickBooks Online.

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:10.063
If you've ever fixed QuickBooks one transaction at a time, BulkAuto does it in

00:00:10.063 --> 00:00:10.370
bulk.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.450
Here's a sample company.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.430
Every tool is on the left.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:17.990
Step one:

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:18.980
the Health scan.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.735
The Health scan checks your books for common problems.

00:00:23.735 --> 00:00:25.470
First, pick the dates.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.630
It shows how much it will read before it starts.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.958
Then click Run scan.

00:00:31.958 --> 00:00:35.853
The scan only reads your books; it never changes anything.

00:00:35.853 --> 00:00:37.800
We've sped this part up.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.515
Here's what it found:

00:00:41.515 --> 00:00:48.217
two hundred uncategorized expenses, about a hundred seventy-four thousand dollars in payments never deposited,

00:00:48.217 --> 00:00:50.610
and sixty-five groups of duplicates.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:56.563
Each problem has a button that opens the right tool, with the problem already

00:00:56.563 --> 00:00:56.916
selected.

00:00:56.916 --> 00:00:59.030
Let's fix them one by one.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.200
First, undeposited payments.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.416
When a customer pays, QuickBooks holds the money in Undeposited Funds until you record

00:01:08.416 --> 00:01:09.470
the bank deposit.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:16.600
Here, ninety-nine payments are still waiting, but twenty-five of them already reached the bank.

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:21.065
That means the income is counted twice.

00:01:21.065 --> 00:01:24.145
BulkAuto pairs each payment with its bank deposit.

00:01:24.145 --> 00:01:25.300
Type to confirm.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:31.695
Each payment moves into the deposit that already recorded it, so the income is

00:01:31.695 --> 00:01:32.356
counted once.

00:01:32.356 --> 00:01:36.320
The bank deposits stay the same, so your bank reconciliation isn't affected.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:41.118
The remaining payments go into one new deposit.

00:01:41.118 --> 00:01:43.470
Choose the bank account and the date.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:50.040
Seventy-four payments, over a hundred thousand dollars, deposited in seconds.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.230
Next, uncategorized expenses.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:58.303
Expenses that were never given a category land in an account called Ask My

00:01:58.303 --> 00:01:58.644
Accountant.

00:01:58.644 --> 00:02:00.690
Reclassify them opens all of them.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.560
There are two hundred and one here.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.760
Instead of editing each one, we'll pick a group and move them all at

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:09.060
once.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.463
The filter panel narrows the list.

00:02:13.463 --> 00:02:18.138
Here, we search the payees for fuel and keep only our fuel vendors, which

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.140
leaves eight charges.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:25.001
Then choose the category they belong in:

00:02:25.001 --> 00:02:25.793
Automobile, Fuel.

00:02:25.793 --> 00:02:28.960
This one choice applies to every selected line.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:35.206
Type to confirm, and all eight lines move together.

00:02:35.206 --> 00:02:38.030
Your reports for those dates update right away.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.510
Next, duplicate transactions.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:47.923
Duplicates happen when the same bill or expense is entered twice, often once by

00:02:47.923 --> 00:02:49.980
hand and once by the bank feed.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:58.421
BulkAuto finds transactions with the same type, payee, date and amount.

00:02:58.421 --> 00:03:01.890
Here, sixty-five groups, with sixty-seven extra copies.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:08.150
You can review any group before deleting, and BulkAuto always keeps one copy.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:15.314
Like every change in BulkAuto, deleting asks you to type a confirmation, and saves

00:03:15.314 --> 00:03:16.410
a backup first.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.780
All sixty-seven duplicates, removed.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.730
Next, old unbilled time.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:29.167
Unbilled time entries from years ago clutter your reports and invoices.

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:29.534
Tip:

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:32.470
press Control K to jump to any screen.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.840
Load the unbilled time for the dates you want to clean up.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:44.365
The totals show the number of entries, the hours and the amount, and the

00:03:44.365 --> 00:03:46.900
breakdown shows them by year and by employee.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:54.817
Use the filters to narrow the list by employee, customer, dates or hours.

00:03:54.817 --> 00:03:58.200
Here, we narrow it down to the older entries.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:04.750
When the list looks right, type the confirmation and delete.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.706
More than two thousand entries, cleared in about a minute and a half.

00:04:11.706 --> 00:04:13.810
Time you've already billed is never touched.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:17.140
Changed your mind?

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:22.790
Every change BulkAuto makes is listed in History, newest first.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.770
Open any run to see exactly what it changed.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:31.821
Then undo it.

00:04:31.821 --> 00:04:35.420
BulkAuto restores everything from the backup it saved before the change.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.170
Every deleted time entry comes back.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.815
History can also export a change log:

00:04:45.815 --> 00:04:50.964
a PDF or spreadsheet of everything you changed, ready to send to your client

00:04:50.964 --> 00:04:51.700
or accountant.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:59.020
It lists every change, with the value before and after.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.660
Finally, the result.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.600
Run the Health scan again.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.899
The duplicate transactions now show as OK.

00:05:09.899 --> 00:05:13.470
Every other finding is one click away from its fix.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:20.250
Try BulkAuto free for five days at getbulkauto.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:20.744
com.
